stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> LifeDispatch
  LifeDispatch --> Suppressed: dead/unconscious/client/anchored/no clients or movement gates
  LifeDispatch --> Feeding: hunger branch takes priority
  LifeDispatch --> Behaviour: handle_ai throttle permits
  Behaviour --> Wandering: wander/scared
  Behaviour --> Idle: hunt/defends/hostile combat handler
  Behaviour --> Alert: enters handler with ALERT stance
  Idle --> Attack: FindTarget selects valid target
  Alert --> Idle: lost target long enough
  Alert --> Attack: stance threshold / hostile
  Attack --> Tired: hunt mode stance_step reaches fatigue threshold
  Tired --> Attack: rested / target present
  Tired --> Idle: rested / no target
  Attack --> Idle: LoseTarget
  Attack --> Attack: pursuit, cover, attack, surroundings
  Feeding --> LifeDispatch: next Life dispatch
  Wandering --> LifeDispatch: next Life dispatch
  Suppressed --> LifeDispatch: next Life dispatch
  note right of Attack
    Simplified stance abstraction.
    Attack methods and NPC types override behavior.
    Native walks/pathfinding also run between Life calls.
  end note
